---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import ArticleCards from '../components/ArticleCards.astro';
import {archive,collections} from '../lib/archive';
import StoryCards from '../components/StoryCards.astro';
import ReaderJourneys from '../components/ReaderJourneys.astro';
import '../styles/stories.css';
import {Image} from 'astro:assets';
import indigoStudy from '../assets/indigo-study.png';
---
<Site title="Yorùbá Stories & Living Memories" active="Overview">
<section class="hero wrap"><div><p class="kicker">PEOPLE · PLACES · LANGUAGE · MEMORY</p><h1>Every town has a tale.<br/><em>What did yours tell you?</em></h1><p class="lead">Enter Yorùbá tales, surprising mysteries, living memories, beliefs and different versions of the stories people grew up hearing.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/tales/">Explore living stories <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button secondary" href="/articles/">Explore the scholars’ archive</a></div><p class="fine">Stories first. Your community’s voice matters. This remains a private preview.</p></div><figure class="home-editorial-cover"><a href="/stories/adire-indigo-design/" aria-label="Read the featured Àdìrẹ story"><Image src={indigoStudy} alt="Original gouache-style illustration of folded indigo cloth and loose threads; an invented textile study, not a documented design." width={640} widths={[320,480,640,900]} sizes="(max-width:650px) calc(100vw - 40px), (max-width:1000px) 45vw, 520px" format="webp" quality={75} loading="eager"/></a><figcaption><p class="kicker">FEATURED STORY · EDITORIAL RESEARCH DRAFT</p><h2><a href="/stories/adire-indigo-design/">The part the blue<br/><em>cannot reach.</em></a></h2><p>Àdìrẹ, design and the intelligence of making.</p><p class="fine">Original AI-generated illustration · not a photograph or historic cloth.</p></figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="wrap notice" aria-labelledby="figures-entry"><p class="kicker">WHO IS WHO IN YORÙBÁ BELIEF AND HISTORY?</p><h2 id="figures-entry">Meet the names behind the tales.</h2><p>Discover what people believe about Èṣù, Olódùmarè, Ọ̀ṣun, Ògún, Ṣàngó and other figures—or learn about the lives and legends of Yorùbá heroes. Clear introductions come first; detailed research stays in its own archive.</p><a href="/figures/">Explore Beliefs, Òrìṣà &amp; Historical Figures →</a></section><section class="wrap section editorial-home-intro" aria-labelledby="home-stories"><div class="section-title"><div><p class="kicker">THE DOCUMENTARY EDITION · ORIGINAL RESEARCH DRAFTS</p><h2 id="home-stories">Begin with a detail.<br/><em>Stay for the story.</em></h2></div><p class="muted">A face without a recovered name. A line the dye cannot reach. Follow four longer readings into objects, making, performance and the care of place.</p></div><StoryCards featured/><p class="home-story-link"><a class="text-link" href="/stories/">All stories and reading journeys →</a></p></section>
<section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="home-journeys"><div class="section-title"><div><p class="kicker">FIVE READINGS AT A TIME</p><h2 id="home-journeys">Follow your curiosity.</h2></div><p class="muted">Each journey connects original archive entries and clearly labelled editorial drafts, with context for the next reading.</p></div><ReaderJourneys/></section>
<section class="wrap section"><div class="section-title"><div><p class="kicker">A PLACE TO BEGIN</p><h2>Follow a thread.</h2></div><p class="muted">Browse the existing collections, then read the evidence behind each account.</p></div><div class="collection-grid">{collections.map((c,i)=><a class="collection" href={`/collections/${c.id}/`}><span class="kicker">0{i+1} / {c.articles.length} readings</span><h3>{c.title}</h3><p>{c.intro}</p><span class="text-link">Open collection ↗</span></a>)}</div></section>
<section class="wrap section"><div class="section-title"><div><p class="kicker">MEMORY & MATERIAL EVIDENCE</p><h2>Begin with questions.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/articles/">All 113 readings →</a></div><ArticleCards articles={['how-we-know','ile-ife','heritage'].map(id=>archive.articles.find(a=>a.id===id)!)}/></section>
<section class="wrap notice"><h2>A source is a starting point.</h2><p>This archive preserves research drafts. A citation does not mean every claim has been independently checked. Community traditions, scholarly interpretation and scientific evidence must retain their distinct contexts.</p><a href="/about/">Read the editorial limits →</a></section>
<section class="wrap notice" aria-labelledby="places-discovery"><p class="kicker">TOWNS, RECORDS AND LOCAL PERSPECTIVES</p><h2 id="places-discovery">Places &amp; Perspectives</h2><p>Follow a new Abẹ́òkúta documentary reading and return to town-specific sections in the preserved archive. Research drafts, private review only.</p><a class="places-discovery-link" href="/places/">Explore Places &amp; Perspectives</a></section>
</Site>
